  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">TZ BetterTomorrow-Disrupt Employment Gap</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Men with disabilities are about twice as likely as women with disabilities to have employment. Women with disabilities confront unfair hiring and promotion criteria, unequal access to training and retraining, unequal access to credit and other productiveresources, and they rarely have a vote in economic decisions when they work. There are also disparities in the labor force between women withvarious types of disability, thus some groups participate at a higher or lower rate than others. Women with disabilities are more likely to be treated unfairly because they are female and have a disability. Many of them are mistreated because they are impoverished. Women with disabilities frequently endure double or even triple discrimination, which is often neglected or unnoticed because people with impairments are sometimes viewed as if they do not have a gender. It is also largely neglected because little is known about its magnitude or effects.

As a result, the organization &quot;A Better Tomorrow&quot; must begin by raising awareness and holding seminars to bring the private and public sectors together. This will be done in collaboration with several commercial sector parties. Also, our organization intends to engage women with disabilities, recruit them, and train them on activities that will prepare them for self-employment after a year of being supported with seed capital or and supported by our organization to obtain a loan from a financial institution or a local government fund. Sewing, designing, knitting, building, learning to use computers, driving a three-wheeler for transportation business, and so on are all activities advised by women with disabilities during our past involvement with them. In addition, our company intends to initiate, design, and organizeacampaign to close the job disability gap, as well as provide mentorship and coaching to all five categories of women with disabilities based on their trained soft skills. Provision of startup funding as well as assistance in obtaining further capital fromfinancial institutions and government loans.

Among the activities that will be implemented include;

Activity 1: Project Inceptioin kick off

Activity 2: raising awareness and conducting seminars to get both the private and public sectors on the same page. This will be done in partnership with different private sector stakeholders

Activity 3: engage women with disabilities, recruit and they will be trained on activities which will enable them after a short period of one year to get ready forself-employment after being supported with seed capital or and supported by our organization to get the loan from the financial institution or LGAs fund

Activity 4: Initiate, design and organise a closing employment disability gap campaign

Activity5: provision of mentorship and coaching to all 5 groups of women with disabilities based on their trained soft skills

Activity 6: Provision of seed capital and support them to get additional capital from financial institutions and government loans</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="4" type="24">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Better Tomorrow was established in 2019 as a network with the mission of educating and informing the Tanzanian mainland population about climate change, gender equality, and other social and economic issues, as well as helping women and young people in the labor force. They also started off as a strong youth network, assisting young people in gaining financial literacy, life and leadership skills, access to sexual and reproductive health care, and self-confidence.Better Tomorrow has &#xa0;been going strong for quite some time,and&#xa0;seen the wonderful benefits the&#xa0;organization has had on the community. As more women expressed interest in becoming members of our group, BT&#xa0;decided to register it. Better TomorroW is a non-profit organization that works on gender equality, economic inequality, and other social issues by involving young people and women on a national and worldwide scale. BT&apos;s&#xa0;objectives include promoting equal participation and benefit from available resources, particularly credit, water, education and health facilities, land, and newdevelopment opportunities; advocating for and raising awareness on various campaigns with initiatives to promote economic activities among youths; empowering youth and the community at large on issues relating to youthrights, climate change, gender-based violence, and education; and promoting the dissemination of information.  Better Tomorrow&apos;s mission is to create a society where women and young people have the power to realize their full potential and can do so by fighting for their legal rights. Additionally, we want to become the leading organization in the battle for gender equality and for giving all women and young girls a safe environment withthe intention of promoting self-reliance, self-assurance, and self-determination. Furthermore, BT&apos;s&#xa0; main goals are gender equalityand women&apos;s empowerment, which we think can both be accomplished successfully if girls and women are granted economic freedom. One of many objectives BT&#xa0;have is this. The goal of this programis to increase the economic potential of young girls who are most in need. Establishing economic independence, granting access to resources, and protecting people from the danger of violence are our goals.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Better Tomorrow</narrative>
